{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":971425,"duration_api_ms":1007369,"num_turns":104,"result":"All implementation steps are complete. Here's the execution payload:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Normalized algae kinetics to use concentration-based (mg/L) half-saturation constants instead of legacy tank-total parameters. Renamed `algae_half_saturation_n_mg_total` → `algae_half_saturation_n_mg_n_per_l` (default 0.25 mg N/L) and `algae_half_saturation_p_mg_total` → `algae_half_saturation_p_mg_p_per_l` (default 0.04 mg P/L) across ProcessParams, ProcessParamsPreset, default.toml, and tank_scenarios. Removed `legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l` conversion from algae_growth.rs—parameters are now used directly as concentrations. Added comprehensive doc comments to `step_daily_algae` explaining light, nutrient (Monod/Liebig), and temperature (Gaussian) interactions, plus notes on what is intentionally abstracted for Phase 1. Added 5 new tests: tank-size independence with different geometries, hand-computed limitation factor verification, temperature sensitivity at one sigma, light-off biomass decline, and phosphorus limitation. All 8 baseline scenario envelopes pass unchanged.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Rename algae half-saturation fields in ProcessParams from legacy _mg_total to _mg_n_per_l / _mg_p_per_l with concentration-based defaults (0.25, 0.04) and serde aliases for backwards compatibility\",\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Remove legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l conversion from algae_growth.rs; use ProcessParams concentration fields directly. Add doc comments documenting light × nutrient × temperature interactions and intentionally abstracted Phase 1 simplifications\",\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Update ProcessParamsPreset in presets.rs: rename fields with serde aliases, update defaults to concentration values (0.25, 0.04), update provenance normalization from LegacyMgPerL to None, update field lookup keys and provenance list entries\",\n      \"order\": 3,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Update default.toml field names and values from legacy totals (5.0, 0.8) to concentration (0.25, 0.04)\",\n      \"order\": 4,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Update UNITS.md to mark algae renames as done (tanksim-6e5.2.5)\",\n      \"order\": 5,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add tank-size-independence test (algae_size_independence_different_geometries): two tanks with different fill heights but identical concentrations produce identical suspended-algae growth\",\n      \"order\": 6,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add hand-computed limitation product test (algae_growth_matches_hand_computed_limitation_product): verifies suspended biomass after one step matches expected value from light_factor × temp_factor × nutrient_factor × max_rate\",\n      \"order\": 7,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add temperature sensitivity test (algae_temperature_one_sigma_below_reduces_growth): gross growth ratio at T_opt − σ vs T_opt matches exp(−0.5)\",\n      \"order\": 8,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add light-off test (algae_light_off_causes_biomass_decline): disabled light → zero gross growth, biomass declines by exactly respiration fraction\",\n      \"order\": 9,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add phosphorus limitation test (algae_phosphorus_limits_growth_below_nitrogen_potential): P-depleted tank grows substantially less than P-rich tank with identical nitrogen\",\n      \"order\": 10,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validation_evidence\": [\n    \"cargo test -p tank_core --test plant_algae_integration: 13/13 passed (including 5 new algae tests + 1 existing volume-invariance test + 7 existing plant tests)\",\n    \"cargo test -p tank_core --test concentration_helpers: 11/11 passed\",\n    \"cargo test -p tank_core --test budget_tracking: 24/24 passed\",\n    \"cargo test -p tank_core --test tank_size_thermal_response: 3/3 passed\",\n    \"cargo test -p tank_data: all tests passed (preset deserialization, provenance, validation)\",\n    \"cargo test -p tank_scenarios: 9/9 passed (scenario materialization with new param names)\",\n    \"cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_baseline_scenarios: 8/8 passed (nano_cycle, medium_planted, warm_room envelopes all within bounds — behaviour unchanged after normalization)\",\n    \"cargo build: clean compilation (only pre-existing warnings from concurrent snapshot.rs changes)\",\n    \"No nutrient limitation term references raw tank totals — algae_growth.rs uses ConcentrationView for nutrients and ProcessParams concentration fields for half-saturation constants directly\"\n  ],\n  \"outstanding_risks\": [\n    \"Pre-existing test failure in snapshot_deserializes_legacy_chemistry_aliases (from concurrent tanksim-6e5.2.4 plant param migration, not caused by this change)\",\n    \"Pre-existing clippy warnings in snapshot.rs (unused serde imports) and water.rs (dead code) from concurrent changes — not introduced by this bead\",\n    \"Serde alias allows old field names to deserialize but the VALUE semantics changed (old: mg in 20L reference, new: mg/L). Saved states using old field names will be misinterpreted as mg/L values, producing very high half-saturation constants. This is acceptable in Phase 1 active development; production save migration would need explicit value conversion\",\n    \"Algae P cycle is intentionally not closed (documented in step_daily_algae comments). Model over-indexes on N limitation until P cycling is completed in a later phase\"\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reaso